@startuml ui_class
title plogic - UI / CLI

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide empty members

interface UI {
  +receive_file(path: str)
  +receive_proposition(proposition: str)
  +start_interactive()
  +present(table: TruthTable)
}

class CLI

class Orchestrator

class TruthTable

note bottom of CLI
  The only impure component. It parses the command
  line (-p, -a, -i, -s, -m, -o, -h, -V and their long
  forms in ui.md), renders the help screen from the
  argument definitions, reads and writes files and
  prints. Help/version are clap's: they print in
  argument order and exit 0. Dash-prefixed arguments
  are options; -- ends option parsing. Usage errors
  print the message and the full help screen and exit
  with code 2;
  I/O problems are reported directly and are outside
  the Error model (ADR-014), with exit code 1.
end note

note bottom of UI
  present() prints, in order: the simplified formula
  (when simplification ran, the default), optionally
  the Proceso: list with -m (omitted when no law
  applied), the aligned truth table, and always the
  classification line, with a blank line between items.
  With --no-simplificar the first line is omitted and
  the table is the original. With --simplificar only
  the Simplificada: line and its optional Proceso:
  block are printed, with no table and no classification.
  Interactive sessions never redirect; every
  non-interactive run may redirect to plogic-output.txt
  when a table exceeds 1024 rows (never with
  --simplificar). In a terminal, only the
  V/F cells of the table are colored (V green, F red);
  the message of an error is bright red on stderr;
  file output is plain.

  The table is left-aligned with two spaces between
  columns and | before the result column, and no
  trailing spaces; a table with no variables has no |.
  File mode numbers its tables ("Proposición n:") and
  separates them with a blank line; interactive mode
  separates a table or an error from the next prompt
  with a blank line (ADR-045). The process lines read
  "n. <law>: <formula>" (ADR-047).
end note

CLI ..|> UI
CLI --> Orchestrator

Orchestrator ..> TruthTable : with_display

UI ..> TruthTable : <<use>>

@enduml
